  "compatibility": {
    "proposed": "backward-compatible",
    "basis": "The v1 SlotSelection is retained unchanged as AgentSlotSelection; all other existing definitions and top-level validation rules are unchanged. Only v2 consumers may accept native selections.",
    "decisionAuthority": "ContractGate",
    "approved": false
  },
  "semanticChecks": [
    "Validate native executor identity, exact implementation and declared absence of model/agent/harness dispatch against the pinned binding catalog and host capabilities; the native tag is a claim to validate, never authority.",
    "Apply the same exact Module ports, outcomes, ordered adapter bindings, required Gates, contributor support, explicit overview, grants, context and effect-checkpoint checks to both branches.",
    "Every native slot contains agents:[] and harness:null; agent-bearing slots retain the exact v1 shape without an execution field. No fallback or fabricated no-op agent is allowed.",
    "Native execution does not imply purity or zero effects. ModulePlugin execution mode and capability grants still govern effects and durable replay.",
    "Single-operation Modules without adapterChain use composition-only stepId terminal and stepOrder 0 for their one binding; materialization must emit the existing single invocation shape with no chain step. Chained operations retain their exact declared step IDs and order.",
    "A native single-operation selection rejects multiple bindings for that operation, nonterminal step IDs, or nonzero step order. The resolver derives single-versus-chain form from the exact ModuleDefinition, never from caller choice.",
    "Native/agent replacement requires a newly preflighted successor run with exact predecessor lineage; existing v1 artifacts and active runs retain their original schema identity and bytes."
  ],
